## US-001: Add an offline fake Hermes process for CLI tests

Date: 2026-11-22
Status: DONE

### What changed
- Created `test/fake-hermes/hermes` -- shell wrapper (like
  fake-claude) whose basename makes spawnAgent take the hermes
  branch
- Created `test/mock-agent-hermes.js` -- Node script that:
  - Validates required Hermes flags (--yolo chat --query-file
    - --quiet) and exits 2 on mismatch
  - Records argv, cwd, and stdin to files via FAKE_HERMES_*
    env vars
  - Success mode: creates and commits a file
  - Nonzero exit mode: exits with FAKE_HERMES_EXIT code, no
    commit
  - No-work mode: exits 0 without committing
    (FAKE_HERMES_NO_WORK=1)
  - Coordinated-wait mode: signals readiness via
    FAKE_HERMES_READY_FILE, blocks until FAKE_HERMES_WAIT_FILE
    appears, then commits
  - Emits stdout/stderr markers via FAKE_HERMES_OUTPUT and
    FAKE_HERMES_STDERR
- Created `test/hermes.test.ts` with 40 assertions covering
  all modes, flag validation, recording, isolation, identity,
  and sharding independence
- Added `hermes` to TESTS in `scripts/test.sh`

### Patterns and gotchas
- macOS /var is a symlink to /private/var, so cwd comparisons
  need realpathSync
- tapzero has no t.pass() -- use t.ok(true, ...) instead
- The FAKE_HERMES_KEYS list must be kept in sync with new env
  vars (same pattern as FAKE_CLAUDE_KEYS in integration tests)
- Pre-existing failures in integration shards 13/20 and 14/20
  are unrelated to this change (confirmed by running clean main)

